<article class="env-lemma" id="0EB1">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0EB1">Lemma <span data-tag="0EB1">51.16.1</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a Noetherian ring of dimension $d$. Let $I \subset I' \subset A$ be ideals. If $I'$ is contained in the Jacobson radical of $A$ and $\text{cd}(A, I') < d$, then $\text{cd}(A, I) < d$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/0DXC" data-tag="0DXC">51.4.7</a> we know $\text{cd}(A, I) \leq d$. We will use Lemma <a href="/tag/0DWV" data-tag="0DWV">51.2.6</a> to show 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  H^ d_{V(I')}(A) \to H^ d_{V(I)}(A)  \]
</div>
    <p>
       is surjective which will finish the proof. Pick $\mathfrak p \in V(I) \setminus V(I')$. By our assumption on $I'$ we see that $\mathfrak p$ is not a maximal ideal of $A$. Hence $\dim (A_\mathfrak p) < d$. Then $H^ d_{\mathfrak pA_\mathfrak p}(A_\mathfrak p) = 0$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/0DXC" data-tag="0DXC">51.4.7</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>